<title>UK: Share buyback rule to save UK up to 400 mln stg/yr.</title>
<headline>Share buyback rule to save UK up to 400 mln stg/yr.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A UK government decision to cancel tax credits on share buybacks, announced on Tuesday, will net savings for the Exchequer of up to 400 million stg a year in tax credit payments from 1998/99.</p>
<p>The Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said in a statement that the change would produce an estimated yield for the Exchequer of 80 million stg in 1996/97 and 200 million stg in 1997/98 building up to 400 million stg per year for 1998/99 onwards.</p>
<p>The changes, which also cover special dividend payouts related to share buybacks take effect from today.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 71 542 7717</p>
</text>
